  description: "A flat, shell-like dish of a plant with uneven dimensions. It grows
    almost entirely sideways, pressed flat against whatever it's rooted to. The only
    cultivar in the Institute\u2019s collection bred to grip stone rather than root
    in soil, you\u2019ll find it clinging sideways to greenhouse walls more often
    than sitting in a pot.\n"
  descriptionSecondary: Used to build paths and ledges when flight is no longer possible.
